SN CPS Gauge v1.0

A cute addition to the output of CNet's CPS measurement after a transfer!
This displays the CPS for the last file, evaluates it and checks to see
if it breaks the previous record.  (Records are kept for each baudrate.)

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)  Also, it would be a good
    idea to put it in it's own directory as it creates alot of it's own
    files (depending on the range of baudrates on your system).

 2  Load up your bbstext into your favorite editor and jump to line #576
    and replace what's on that line with the following:

    {#0SN:CPSGauge/SN_CPSGauge %d}

    Modify the path to suit and remember, \ = CTRL-Y and { = CTRL-Q.

 3  Reload your bbstext/bbsmenu via CNet's Control Panel menu (option
    #3, "Text/menu reload  RAmiga-T" and you're all set!

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

